<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38087" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praeter-lābor</span></b> , lapsus, 3,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. dep. n.</i>
			and <i>a.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>to glide</i> or <i>flow by</i>, <i>to fly</i> or <i>run past</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praeterlabentia flumina,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 10, 3, 24</span></i>
			.—With <i>acc.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tumulum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 6, 874</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hanc (tellurem) pelago praeterlabare necesse
					est,</span>”
				<i>to sail past</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 3, 478</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to slip away</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(definitio) ante praeterlabitur, quam percepta
					est,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. de Or. 2, 25, 109</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
